  <h2 class="method-head">Prototype methodology</h2>
  <p class="wire-note">These gauges use illustrative thresholds to demonstrate the dashboard. Replace them with your own system's rules before launch.</p>
  <ul class="method-list">
    <li><strong>Trend Regime</strong> — SPY vs its 50- and 200-day moving averages. Bullish above both, bearish below both, neutral when mixed.</li>
    <li><strong>Momentum</strong> — 63-trading-day S&amp;P 500 return. Bullish above +5%, bearish below −5%.</li>
    <li><strong>Realized Volatility</strong> — 20-day annualized standard deviation of SPY returns, computed with the population standard deviation (the full 20-day window, not a sample estimate). Bullish under 14%, bearish over 22%.</li>
    <li><strong>Yield Curve</strong> — 10-year minus 2-year Treasury yield (FRED). Bullish over +0.25pp, bearish under −0.25pp.</li>
    <li><strong>Inflation</strong> — CPI year-over-year (FRED). Bullish under 2.5%, bearish over 3.5%.</li>
    <li><strong>Labor</strong> — Unemployment rate and 3-month change (FRED). Bearish if up 0.3pp or more in 3 months.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="wire-note">Sources: Massive (price history), FRED (macro series). Computed at build time; refresh with <code>npm run signals</code>.</p>
</section>
